  "title": "Rigidity at the Ideal Endpoint for Equiangular Hyperbolic 4-Cubes",
  "batch_label": "79",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Every full-dimensional finite-volume convex hyperbolic 4-polytope whose face lattice is that of the 4-cube, whose vertices are finite or ideal (with no hyperideal or truncated substitute), and whose dihedral angles all equal alpha_0 = arccos(1/3), is isometric to the regular ideal equiangular 4-cube C^4_(alpha_0), represented in the Klein ball by the closure [-1/2,1/2]^4.",
